What is the output of a switch statement when no break is used between cases?
int day = 2;
switch (day) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Monday");
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Tuesday");
    case 3:
        System.out.println("Wednesday");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Invalid day");
}
A. The output will be Tuesday only.
B. The output will be Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday.
C. The output will be Tuesday and Wednesday.
D. The code will fail to compile.
